WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:02.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I want to talk
about some good news.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.203 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Boris Johnson,

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
out of the woods.
-Yes. Yes.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:08.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The Queen actually
gave an address.

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:10.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is very rare.
-Yes.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:16.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was it a tonic
for you to see the Queen speak

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.084 line:92%
-I mean, what kind of tonic?

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.653
One of those tonics that you
think is going to do something

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:22.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
you rub it on you,
and you realize,

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.757 line:92%
"Oh, no, that didn't do it"?

00:00:23.757 --> 00:00:24.824 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:25.592 line:92%
-Like an expensive tonic,

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
like something from Goop,
where you just go --

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:29.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, or maybe like
a gin and tonic,

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.231 line:92%
but the tonic's a little flat.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:33.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
That's exactly it.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:34.300 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay, gotcha.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.636
-You know, 'cause normally the
Queen speaks every Christmas

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:40.106
And if the Queen is speaking
at a time that isn't Christmas

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's not because
things are going well.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's because Princess Diana
just died,

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.946 line:92%
or the country is at war.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:48.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-That's basically it.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.116 size:88% position:44% line:92%
So, the Queen turning up

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
in itself
is not a reassuring thing.

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.187 line:92%
If it's a message from the Queen

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:56.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's not
"Happy Christmas, everyone,"

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:58.858 size:81% position:41% line:92%
then that's not great.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:03.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, yeah, I hope, for thos
whom she could calm down,

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.298 line:92%
I hope she calmed them down.

00:01:05.298 --> 00:01:06.933 size:81% position:41% line:92%
But I don't know if --

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.936 size:84% position:42%
We said on our show,
what was more inspiring

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
was that she was wearing
a green dress,

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:13.206 line:92%
and so everyone in England

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:16.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
just started projecting things
onto the green dress.

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, because
it was a green screen.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.978
It was a natural green screen.
-Yeah, it was a green screen

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:23.483
So, you should never wear gree
in front of a television camer

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:25.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
unless you're happy
to have things --

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:26.419 line:92%
unless you're happy to wea

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
things that people
want you to wear.

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.422 line:92%
And that's -- In a sense,

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Queen learned
a very important lesson,

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:33.426
which is if you don't want
to be dressed like Iron Man,

00:01:33.426 --> 00:01:34.160 line:92%
don't wear a green dress.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.896
-So you don't think this was a
case of her knowing in advance

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.666
like, "Let them -- They'll
have some fun with this"?

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That would be great.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:44.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean, it would be
wildly out of character,

00:01:44.104 --> 00:01:45.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it would be
very generous, right?

00:01:45.839 --> 00:01:47.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like someone choosing a movie
poster

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's begging for a [bleep]
to be drawn on it.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.511 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:54.347 size:78% position:39%
God, I've never been
much of a monarchist,

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.849 line:92%
but I would really appreciate,

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:58.218
like, her coming to the nation's
time of need.

00:01:58.218 --> 00:02:01.921
She goes, "No, I don't
want to go with the blue.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.022 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Give them the green."

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:05.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. "Let them
enjoy themselves."

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Let them enjoy --
Have at it, Britain."

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.062 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:13.533 size:84% position:42%
"This country is at war
with a vicious disease.

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.767 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Have at it."

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:18.238 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:18.238 --> 00:02:19.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the people
that's reassuring

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:23.343 size:88% position:44%
or certainly has brought
some reassurance to many

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:25.578 size:78% position:39% line:92%
is Dr. Anthony Fauci.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:26.012 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:30.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Some say, "How can you stan
there if you're a doctor

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:33.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
and listen to the presiden
say things

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we know are
scientifically untrue?"

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you actually have
some appreciation

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.893 line:92%
for the tough spot he's in

00:02:39.893 --> 00:02:41.594 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah. I mean, yeah.

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:44.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think, when he was
asked a question,

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:45.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
that question,
by a medical journal,

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:50.303
I think his response was, right,
"What would you have me do?"

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.638 line:92%
'cause I get, you could have him

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:54.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
just cough "Bull[bleep]"
or into your sleeve,

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
not into your hand.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:59.746 line:92%
-"Bull[bleep]. Bull[bleep]

00:02:59.746 --> 00:03:02.248 line:92%
But, yeah, but that would mean

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:03.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he couldn't
do his job anymore,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think there's
nothing more important

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:10.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
than him doing his job
as long as he possibly can

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.258 line:92%
And so he's going to need

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
to draw on internal
reserves of discipline

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I certainly
don't have access to.

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:18.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, we're very lucky
not to be in a situation

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:21.834
where we have to nod along
with people we disagree with

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.736 line:92%
-That's right. His biggest tel

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
is just kind of slightly -
just doing that.

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:28.074 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:30.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Rather than just the full
"What the [bleep]"

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:33.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's like he's slowing down
a face slap.

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:37.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like a --
-That's right. That's right.

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:38.885 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Just --

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:41.287 line:92%
Not just the full, "Oh, God.

00:03:41.287 --> 00:03:42.288 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:47.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"I'm so good at my job.
How can he be so bad at his?

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much
for making time for us.

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:50.230 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I really appreciate it.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks for doing your show
through all this.

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:54.934
-Congratulations to Alexi
on the flower arrangements

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.169 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's nice to see.

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:56.970 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:58.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I know
as soon as this is over

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:02.675
you re-scrub those walls to keep
them that way, and you're --

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:03.876 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:06.746 line:92%
-Full "Karate Kid." Wax on -

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:08.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
Wipe on.
-Thanks, John.

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:09.048 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Wipe off.

00:04:09.048 --> 00:04:11.718
-We'll see you back
in the studio next time, I hope.

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:13.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Chuckles ]
Sure, I'll see you in 2021

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
John Oliver, everybody.

